	"nodes":[
		{"id":"425ab03ddffb18a2","x":-125,"y":179,"width":571,"height":1012,"type":"file","file":"Lessen/HAVO 3/Lesplannen/Week 44/Chapter 1 Test Information.md"},
		{"id":"573a53e07c08edfe","type":"text","text":"# **Today's Class**","x":86,"y":-108,"width":228,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1be9587cf6029f8a","type":"text","text":"### Questions & Negations : Quick Overview\n\n**1. Already have _to be_ or an auxiliary verb?**  \nUse that verb.\n\n- She **is** working. → **Is** she working?\n- She **is** working. → She **isn't** working.\n- He **can** swim. → **Can** he swim?\n\n**2. No auxiliary verb?**  \nUse **do / does / did**.\n\n- You play. → **Do** you play?\n- She plays. → **Does** she play?\n- He played. → **Did** he play?\n\n**3. Negatives**\n\n- I **don't** play.\n- She **doesn't** play.\n- He **didn't** play.\n\n**4. Important:**  \nAfter **do / does / did**, always use the **infinitive**.\n\nCorrect: **Did he go?**  \nWrong: _Did he went?_","x":797,"y":-30,"width":492,"height":758,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"6b9fce4f90291122","type":"text","text":"### Tenses: Quick Overview\n\n**Present simple**  \nHabit / fact\n\n- I **play** football.\n- She **plays** football.\n\n**Present continuous**  \nHappening now\n\n- I **am playing**.\n- She **is playing**.\n- They **are playing**.\n\n**Past simple**  \nFinished action in the past\n\n- I **played** football.\n- She **went** home.\n\n**Past continuous**  \nAction in progress in the past\n\n- I **was playing**.\n- They **were playing**.\n\n### Quick rule\n\n- **Present simple** = usually / always\n- **Present continuous** = happening now\n- **Past simple** = finished past action\n- **Past continuous** = was happening","x":1325,"y":-30,"width":352,"height":839,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"fca9741e3d1dc1eb","type":"text","text":"## 1. Compounds with _some-, any-, every-, no-_\n\nThese combine with:\n\n||**-thing (things)**|**-body / -one (people)**|**-where (places)**|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|**some-**|something|somebody / someone|somewhere|\n|**any-**|anything|anybody / anyone|anywhere|\n|**every-**|everything|everybody / everyone|everywhere|\n|**no-**|nothing|nobody / no one|nowhere|","x":797,"y":-454,"width":880,"height":346,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7553766ad9be496e","type":"text","text":"## 2. Gerunds and _to + infinitive_\n\n### Gerund\n\n**gerund = verb + -ing**\n\nA gerund is a verb used as a noun.\n\nIt can be used after verbs such as:\n\n- _(dis)like_\n- _love_\n- _miss_\n- _avoid_\n\nExamples:\n- _I love driving along the coast._\n- _We miss running in the park._\n\n### _to + infinitive_\n\nUse **to + infinitive** after:\n\n- verbs such as _hope, ask, refuse, expect_\n- adjectives that express an opinion\n- the object of a sentence","x":797,"y":769,"width":492,"height":663,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"da84af66feb049c5","type":"text","text":"\n## **12:20** -\tChapter 1 Test information\n\n## **12:30** -\tSummative Chapter 1 Test\n\n## **12:50** -\tGrammar or Blooket\n\n## **13:05** -\tWrap-up and Study reminder","x":-124,"y":-29,"width":649,"height":188,"color":"4"}
